  "result": "Orders now have a `refunded` state. All 11 tests pass, 5 of them new, using the README's command `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`shop/orders.py`**: `refunded` is added to the list of states. Paid and shipped orders can move to it, and nothing can move out of it.\n- **`tests/test_orders.py`**: five new tests check that:\n  - paid \u2192 refunded works;\n  - shipped \u2192 refunded works;\n  - new and cancelled orders can't be refunded;\n  - a refunded order can't move to any state;\n  - `sales_by_customer` leaves refunded orders out.\n\n**Left unchanged**\n- **`shop/reports.py`**: `sales_by_customer` only counts orders that are `paid` or `shipped`, so refunded orders are already excluded. The new test checks this, so the report stays correct if that list changes.\n- **Storage, CLI, README and cache**: storage saves the state as a plain value, and the CLI and README don't list states. `cache.py` only caches prices, not sales totals.\n\nNothing is committed.",
